<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Tips for Making Tofu Lettuce Wraps</strong></h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Don&#8217;t skip pressing the tofu.</strong> Removing excess water gives the tofu a better texture and allows it to absorb more of the sauce.  You can use either paper towels and/or a tofu press.</li>



<li><strong>Use the large holes of your grater.</strong> This creates pieces that are small enough to work as a lettuce-wrap filling but still have some texture.</li>



<li><strong>Let the mushrooms cook down.</strong> Mushrooms release quite a bit of water as they cook, so give them time to cook off that moisture before adding the sauce. This helps prevent a watery filling.</li>



<li><strong>Adjust the heat.</strong> If you like things spicy, add more sriracha. If you&#8217;re serving these to someone who isn&#8217;t a fan of heat, start with less.</li>
</ul>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-4 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
