<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Why Grate Tofu?</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you&#8217;ve only ever cubed or sliced tofu, grating it is worth trying. The smaller pieces create more surface area, which means there&#8217;s more opportunity for the sauce to cling to the tofu. Combined with the mushrooms, it creates a filling that&#8217;s flavorful, hearty, and completely different from the crispy tofu cubes I&#8217;ve shared in some of my other tofu recipes. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And that&#8217;s exactly why I&#8217;m continuing this tofu series. There are so many ways to prepare the same food!<strong> </strong>If you haven&#8217;t loved tofu in one preparation, that doesn&#8217;t mean you won&#8217;t like it another way. Sometimes it&#8217;s simply about finding the way <em>you</em> like to eat it. <strong><a href="https://www.amysnutritionkitchen.com/air-fryer-tofu/">Air Fryer Tofu</a></strong> is my go-to way to prepare tofu when I need a quick and easy weeknight dinner. I love adding it to bowls because it&#8217;s so simple to make, and the tofu stays nice and crispy—exactly how I like it! It&#8217;s one of those recipes I can throw together while I&#8217;m preparing the rest of my meal, making it an easy option when I don&#8217;t want dinner to feel like a lot of work.</p>



